{"value_info":{"kind":"Reference","basis":"Syntax","qualifier":"SharedBorrow"},"type_info":{"shape":{"kind":"Indirect","pointer":false,"target":{"kind":"Scalar","name":"String"}},"origin":"Declared","native":"&str"},"id":"crate::domain::order::Order::customer~2","kind":"Method","name":"customer","qualified_name":"crate::domain::order::Order::customer~2","parent":"crate::domain::order::Order","language":"rust","origins":[{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1124,"end_byte":1183,"start_line":50,"start_col":5,"end_line":52,"end_col":6}],"flavors":["from-trait:Priced","&self"],"signature":"fn customer(&self) -> &str","type_text":"&str","has_flow":true,"rust_contract":[{"group":"Function","text":"fn declares a function named customer. The parentheses contain its parameters, and the braces contain its body. Declaring it makes the function available. The body runs when the function is called.","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1124,"end_byte":1126,"start_line":50,"start_col":5,"end_line":50,"end_col":7}},{"group":"Receiver","text":"self names the value on which this method is called, like this in C#. &self borrows that value for shared access while the borrow lasts.","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1136,"end_byte":1141,"start_line":50,"start_col":17,"end_line":50,"end_col":22}},{"group":"Shared receiver","text":"&self means this method receives a shared reference to the value it was called on. The caller keeps ownership; the method borrows that value for access rather than taking it by value. Ordinary fields cannot be changed through this shared reference, although types with interior mutability can permit controlled changes. The reference remains valid only for its borrow's lifetime; multiple shared references can coexist while Rust's borrowing rules are satisfied.","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1136,"end_byte":1141,"start_line":50,"start_col":17,"end_line":50,"end_col":22}},{"group":"Trait implementation","text":"This `impl Priced for Order` says that Order implements the Priced trait. A trait describes a set of behavior or associated items; this block supplies the required items that lack defaults and may override provided defaults for this type. Code can then use Order where Priced is required, subject to the trait's bounds and visibility. The declarations inside the braces are associated with this implementation; the block does not create a Order value.","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1095,"end_byte":1117,"start_line":49,"start_col":1,"end_line":49,"end_col":23}},{"group":"String slice type","text":"Rust's built-in str is a dynamically sized sequence of bytes that must contain valid UTF-8 text. It has no fixed size known at compile time, so it is usually used behind a reference such as &str; that reference describes a borrowed portion of text and carries its length. str is not the same as String, which owns a growable buffer. The meaning of an unqualified name depends on name resolution if a name shadows the built-in type.","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1147,"end_byte":1150,"start_line":50,"start_col":28,"end_line":50,"end_col":31}},{"group":"Shared reference type","text":"&str is a shared reference: it borrows a value of type str instead of taking ownership. Several shared references can coexist. The reference must remain valid for its lifetime; while it is used, ordinary mutation of the borrowed data is restricted, though types with interior mutability can permit controlled changes. A reference does not by itself copy the underlying value.","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1146,"end_byte":1150,"start_line":50,"start_col":27,"end_line":50,"end_col":31}},{"group":"Borrowed string slice","text":"&str is a shared reference to a string slice: it lets code read UTF-8 text stored elsewhere without taking ownership of that text. The reference must not outlive the text it refers to. It points to a sequence of bytes, so byte positions need not correspond to characters and a slice must end at UTF-8 character boundaries. This is a borrowed view, rather than an owned, growable String.","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1146,"end_byte":1150,"start_line":50,"start_col":27,"end_line":50,"end_col":31}},{"group":"Receives","text":"Borrow the receiver for reading","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1136,"end_byte":1141,"start_line":50,"start_col":17,"end_line":50,"end_col":22},"type_info":{"shape":{"kind":"Indirect","pointer":false,"target":{"kind":"Named","name":"self","arguments":[]}},"origin":"Declared","native":"&self"}},{"group":"Returns","text":"A reference to data that must remain available for the required lifetime","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1146,"end_byte":1150,"start_line":50,"start_col":27,"end_line":50,"end_col":31},"type_info":{"shape":{"kind":"Indirect","pointer":false,"target":{"kind":"Scalar","name":"String"}},"origin":"Declared","native":"&str"}},{"group":"Lifetime","text":"The returned reference uses the same lifetime as the reference in &self.","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1146,"end_byte":1150,"start_line":50,"start_col":27,"end_line":50,"end_col":31}},{"group":"Implements","text":"Priced","span":{"file":"src/domain/order.rs","start_byte":1100,"end_byte":1106,"start_line":49,"start_col":6,"end_line":49,"end_col":12},"type_info":{"shape":{"kind":"Named","name":"Order","arguments":[]},"origin":"Declared","native":"Order"}}]}
