s about 15–17 significant decimal digits of precision, not a fixed number of digits after the decimal point. Many decimal fractions cannot be represented exactly, so arithmetic can round; it also supports positive and negative infinity and NaN. Rust does not implicitly convert between f32 and f64.","span":{"file":"src/domain/shapes.rs","start_byte":183,"end_byte":186,"start_line":10,"start_col":17,"end_line":10,"end_col":20}}]}
