h `Result` or ShipError type is meant.","span":{"file":"src/main.rs","start_byte":1316,"end_byte":1337,"start_line":41,"start_col":69,"end_line":41,"end_col":90}},{"group":"Unit type","text":"() is the unit type. It has exactly one value, also written (). It commonly indicates that no meaningful result is returned; unlike the never type !, a function returning () can finish normally.","span":{"file":"src/main.rs","start_byte":1323,"end_byte":1325,"start_line":41,"start_col":76,"end_line":41,"end_col":78}},{"group":"Exclusive reference","text":"&mut T is an exclusive reference to a value of type T. It borrows the value rather than taking ownership of it, and permits mutation through this reference. While the borrow is active, other access to the borrowed place is restricted; Rust checks the lifetime and aliasing rules. Reborrowing through this reference is possible, but the original reference is restricted while the reborrow is active.","span":{"file":"src/main.rs","start_byte":1269,"end_byte":1311,"start_line":41,"start_col":22,"end_line":41,"end_col":64}},{"group":"May change","text":"service","span":{"file":"src/main.rs","start_byte":1260,"end_byte":1311,"start_line":41,"start_col":13,"end_line":41,"end_col":64},"type_info":{"shape":{"kind":"Indirect","pointer":false,"target":{"kind":"Named","name":"OrderService","arguments":[{"kind":"Named","name":"InMemoryOrderRepository","arguments":[]}]}},"origin":"Declared","native":"&mut OrderService<InMemoryOrderRepository>"}},{"group":"Returns","text":"Value returned to the caller","span":{"file":"src/main.rs","start_byte":1316,"end_byte":1337,"start_line":41,"start_col":69,"end_line":41,"end_col":90},"type_info":{"shape":{"kind":"Named","name":"Result","arguments":[{"kind":"Scalar","name":"Unit"},{"kind":"Named","name":"ShipError","arguments":[]}]},"origin":"Declared","native":"Result<(), ShipError>"}}]}
